        "id": "moment-target",
        "component": "statistic",
        "section": "context",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "The first moment of the Chebyshev error",
        "contract": "The truncated integral of (ψ(t)−t)/t² from 1 to U tends to −1−γ as U tends to infinity.",
        "idea": "This is an improper-integral limit for the real von Mangoldt sum. It fixes the coefficient of the linear centering term in the reading converse.",
        "assumptions": [],
        "lean_head": "def PsiZeroConst : Prop",
        "declaration": "Formalism.HermitianLattices.GL2a2.PsiZeroConst",
        "module": "Formalism.GL3MeanSquares.PrimeCountAsymptoticInProgressions",
        "url": "https://github.com/Deicyde/riemann-hypothesis/blob/40e56bab026552e089d7afcfeff08d2defb9c005/src/Formalism/GL3MeanSquares/PrimeCountAsymptoticInProgressions.lean#L18-L20",
        "excerpt": "def PsiZeroConst : Prop :=\n  Tendsto (fun U : ℝ => ∫ u in (1 : ℝ)..U, (psumR (fun n => Λ n) u - u) / u ^ 2) atTop\n    (𝓝 (-1 - Real.eulerMascheroniConstant))",
