          "L1": {
            "title": "The Bridge Between Spectrum and Symmetry",
            "headline": "A load-bearing import connects automorphic data to arithmetic symmetry, and everything downstream that reads characters or cohomology windows rests on it.",
            "explanation": "The Galois row is a bridge. On one side are automorphic representations, which are spectral or analytic objects. On the other side are Galois representations, which are symmetries of number fields. The two must agree locally at every good prime. The supply chain has two inputs: a high-rank theta lift that pushes data into large unitary groups, and a weight-one geometric realization that acts as a simple geometric seed. Together they feed a conditional construction whose output is the row.",
            "key_insight": "This is the main bottleneck of the arithmetic stratum. If the bridge fails, both the character interface and the cohomology-window interface lose their foundation.",
            "analogy_anchor": "A load-bearing pillar standing on two foundations, a large lift and a small geometric seed, and supporting two separate floors above.",
            "loss_meter": {
              "fidelity_score": 0.45,
              "compression_ratio": "~50,000:1",
              "topology_status": "faithful_projection",
              "what_is_omitted": [
                "The hypotheses on π (CM field, regularity, algebraicity, polarization through χ)",
                "The contents of PropsB (continuity, semisimplicity, comparisons, weight and Hodge–Tate relations)",
                "The weight and dimension conditions of the theta lift (d ≥ d₀, d + m_W(w) ≤ 2λ_{w,k})",
                "The identity of the downstream consumers everyCharacter_of_row and vwin_of_row"
              ],
              "where_metaphor_breaks": "A pillar is either standing or not. The row is a universally quantified existence statement over all CM fields, primes ℓ, ranks a and representations π, and in this capsule it is wired from named theorems whose own proofs are not pinned here."
            }
          },
          "L2": {
            "title": "Contract: Row0b and Its Producer Wiring",
            "headline": "Input (E CM, ℓ, ι, a ≥ 1, π, χ). Output ∃ (r, wt, HT) with PropsB. The proof is wired from tLiftK and geoOne_holds.",
            "explanation": "Row0b quantifies over a CM number field E with algebraic closure Ω, a prime ℓ with ι : Q̄_ℓ ≃ ℂ, a ≥ 1, cuspidal π on GL_a and a Hecke character χ of the maximal real subfield, where π is regular algebraic and (π, χ) is a polarized pair. It returns r : G(E, Ω) → GL_a(Q̄_ℓ), a weight wt ∈ ℤ and Hodge–Tate multisets HT satisfying PropsB. The wiring is: `galoisLocalGlobalStrong_recParameter` := `galoisRepresentations_of_thetaLift tLiftK`, which itself unfolds to `galoisLocalGlobalStrong_of_geometry_lift geoOne_holds up`. The output crosses interfaces if-01 (everyCharacter_of_row) and if-02 (vwin_of_row).",
            "key_insight": "The producer has no explicit global premise, but only because the premises TLiftK and GeoOne are discharged by named theorems. The real cost sits inside those theorems.",
            "analogy_anchor": "A dependency-injected service: the interface Row0b is satisfied by a constructor that takes two providers, tLiftK and geoOne_holds.",
            "loss_meter": {
              "fidelity_score": 0.7,
              "compression_ratio": "~5,000:1",
              "topology_status": "faithful_projection",
              "what_is_omitted": [
