                "The proofs of tLift_holds_k, weight_one_geometric_realization and galoisLocalGlobalStrong_of_geometry_lift"
              ],
              "where_metaphor_breaks": "Dependency injection suggests the providers are cheap and interchangeable. Here each provider is a deep mathematical theorem, and the wrappers pinned in the capsule show the wiring, not the depth."
            }
          },
          "L3": {
            "title": "Row0b via Unitary Theta Chains and Weight-One Geometric Realization",
            "headline": "Galois representations attached to RAPC π on GL_a/E, obtained by lifting to high-rank unitary groups and realizing geometrically.",
            "explanation": "Row0b asserts, for regular algebraic polarized cuspidal π on GL_a(𝔸_E) with E CM, a continuous semisimple ℓ-adic r whose Frobenius polynomials match the Satake parameters of π, together with weight and Hodge–Tate data (PropsB). The input TLiftK is a theta correspondence for a unitary dual pair. For a Hermitian space X (J = 1) of dimension n and skew-Hermitian spaces W of dimension d ≥ d₀ with J = δ·1, Hecke characters χ_X and χ_W with prescribed restrictions and exponents m_X, m_W, and an automorphic U of weights λ satisfying d + m_W(w) ≤ 2λ_{w,k}, it produces a lift U′ on the rank-d group. GeoOne supplies a weight-one geometric realization, and the conditional theorem `galoisLocalGlobalStrong_of_geometry_lift` combines both inputs into Row0b recT.",
            "key_insight": "The strategy is to move π, by a theta lift, to a high rank where geometry is available, then read off the Galois representation geometrically, using weight one as the base case.",
            "analogy_anchor": "The Kudla–Rallis-style stable-range theta correspondence for unitary dual pairs used as a ramp toward geometric realizations.",
            "loss_meter": {
              "fidelity_score": 0.9,
              "compression_ratio": "~200:1",
              "topology_status": "faithful_projection",
              "what_is_omitted": [
