        "en": {
          "L0": {
            "title": "The quiet stretch of road",
            "headline": "On a long enough road you can always find a stretch where \"ghost letters\" are rare.",
            "explanation": "Picture letters that look fine at every little post office yet never add up to one whole message — \"ghost letters\". This piece promises that on a very long trip you can always find a whole stretch of road, from milestone Y to milestone Y times Y, where the ghost letters stay under a fixed ceiling. That quiet stretch is handed on to the \"hosts\", who build on it.",
            "key_insight": "You don't need silence everywhere; one long, guaranteed quiet stretch is enough.",
            "analogy_anchor": "A night driver looking for a stretch without radio static so one station comes through clearly.",
