                "Internal tower nodes: tower-class-rank, tower-operator-bound, tower-fixed-growth",
                "Details of counts-joint, counts-height, counts-pointwise, counts-inside/outside",
                "Where the prime pairs from interface if-03 (hostThickExists) come from"
              ],
              "where_metaphor_breaks": "The SLA analogy implies an operational guarantee over time; here the \"window\" is a range of scales in an existence theorem, with no algorithm that finds Y and no effective constants J, X0."
            }
          },
          "L3": {
            "title": "The cohomological window: bounding Sha lengths on [Y, Y²]",
            "headline": "Weighted lengths of locally trivial Galois cohomology of twisted modules are ≤ √exp(x^ε), uniformly over the fields.",
            "explanation": "VVle E t B requires that for every algebraic closure Ω and local data LData the lengths shaLen(ld p, e) are finite for 0 < e < t, and that Σ_{ℓ∈S} log ℓ · Σ_{e∈[1,t)} shaLen ≤ B for every finite S. The window comes from a chain: vwin_of_row (Row0b with the IsRecT convention) → automorphic_window_of_inputs (OpenImageCondition, BaseChangeIsobaricN, RowT) → v_window_of_depth_zero_residual_bc_cm (adds the CM abelian inputs) → v_window_of_literal_automorphy_n (rank-N hypothesis) → patching with descWeak → vwin_of_hypotheses_H_E_alt. That last step combines lemma K (lemmaK_litN_alt), ends0_alt and counts i (Kato, unramified automorphy), ii/iii (sp4In) and v (unitary lift) via of_four_alt.",
            "key_insight": "The Sha bound comes from rank-N automorphy plus patching, and the four counts split the twist space into disjoint cases that are each controlled separately.",
