                "The admissible range of epsilon and the existence of the starting threshold x0",
                "How twisted character classes are matched to scales"
              ],
              "where_metaphor_breaks": "A supply line delivers physical goods over time; here nothing is produced step by step: the theorem asserts existence of hosts at all large scales at once, conditional on the window hypothesis."
            }
          },
          "L2": {
            "title": "Host Supply Contract",
            "headline": "Input: VWinAt ψ 401 for each primitive ψ. Output: HostExW (3/2) (GChi ψ).req.",
            "explanation": "The interface from cohomology supplies VWinAt ψ 401; supplyChi turns it into host existence of width 3/2 for the requirement attached to GChi ψ, which is passed to comparison. The proof reduces via supplyOfAdm to showing, for each admissible ε, a threshold x0 beyond which every scale s admits suitable twisted character classes. That obligation is discharged directly by admissibleClassesTwistedChar.",
            "key_insight": "The component is a thin, fully generic adapter: quantify over ψ, then over admissible ε, then over large scales.",
            "analogy_anchor": "An adapter function with signature (ψ, window proof) → host-existence proof.",
            "loss_meter": {
