                "The proof of admissibleClassesTwistedChar itself",
                "The precise bounds on ε encoded by the hypotheses he0 and he1",
                "The upstream proof that VWinAt ψ 401 holds"
              ],
              "where_metaphor_breaks": "An adapter function only reshapes data; this theorem carries mathematical content through admissibleClassesTwistedChar, and its output is a proposition, not computed hosts."
            }
          },
          "L3": {
            "title": "Cyclic Character Hosts via supplyChi",
            "headline": "For every primitive character ψ, VWinAt ψ 401 implies HostExW (3/2) (GChi ψ).req.",
            "explanation": "supplyChi applies supplyOfAdm to ψ and its window hypothesis, reducing host existence to an admissibility statement: for every ε in the admissible range there is x0 such that every scale s of the system beyond x0, with bounds on the parameter φ and level H0, carries admissible twisted character classes. admissibleClassesTwistedChar provides exactly this x0, and the proof closes by substituting the scale equation. The width 3/2 is uniform in ψ, and the window parameter is the fixed constant 401.",
            "key_insight": "All the analytic weight lives in VWinAt (upstream) and admissibleClassesTwistedChar; supplyChi is the uniform-in-ψ glue between them.",
            "analogy_anchor": "A uniform existence statement over primitive characters, obtained by specialising an admissibility lemma.",
