                "The SigA term and its bound sigA_le"
              ],
              "where_metaphor_breaks": "The 'fixed commission' holds only for large enough x (thresholds x1, x2, x3). The comparison says nothing about whether geometric families with eD = 2 and eL = 0 exist; that is supplied by the input interface TopG."
            }
          },
          "L2": {
            "title": "Exponent Choreography in the Comparison Layer",
            "headline": "In: TopG (eD=2, eL=0) and hosts with width 3/2. Out: G_P ≤ x^(1/2+9ε) on windows, sent to the choreography layer.",
            "explanation": "ch_top: for each index u, gapA = ASK(u) − Main(u) ≤ x^(CErr·ε)·errorBracketSizeWindows(x, ε, |H|, |TT|, |T2|, m, b, k, aE). ch_core with C = max(eD+eL, 0) + 3 averages these bounds: GmA ≤ x^(1/2+(C+3)ε) + SigA, under the conditions m ≤ x^(1/2+ε/2) and xm ≤ k. core_gm absorbs the factor 1 + 4o into x^ε and gives Λ.Gm(x) ≤ x^(1/2+(eD+eL+7)ε) for x ≥ x1. windowInequality_of_artinInputs then chooses the threshold max(x1, x0, xE) on each window.",
            "key_insight": "Invariant: the final exponent is linear in (eD, eL) with slope ε, so the input budget fully determines the output budget.",
            "analogy_anchor": "A pipeline: a per-index bound, then averaging, then absorbing constants, then choosing thresholds",
            "loss_meter": {
              "fidelity_score": 0.7,
              "compression_ratio": "~5,000:1",
