          "L3": {
            "title": "Finite Character Comparison on (E0 × H)",
            "headline": "Orthogonality of additive characters on the subgroup A0, the kept characters Kp and the coefficient c = (3o+1)⁻¹ link gapA with GmA.",
            "explanation": "The characters are ell : AddChar(E0 × H) ℂ → ℂ, with the subgroup A0 ⊆ H, the kept set Kp, coefficient c = (3o+1)⁻¹ satisfying |c| ≤ 1, and M = 4o in CharsA. The hypothesis ∀u ∈ A0, gapA(u) ≤ x^(Cε)·bracket, together with ThinScales, CostWindows and RestSize, implies GmA ≤ x^(1/2+(C+3)ε) + SigA. In core_gm the identification gmA_eq takes GmA to Λ.Gm, and SigA is controlled by sigA_le. level_gm_le_on_family_scales sends ChainTied to the shared host data via tiedCore_of_chainTied.",
            "key_insight": "The finite Fourier transform on H with A0 converts a pointwise geometric bound into a bound on a weighted, localized Landau-type prime sum, losing only powers of x^ε.",
            "analogy_anchor": "Discrete Plancherel/orthogonality on a finite abelian group as a translator of inequalities",
