          "L0": {
            "title": "The order of choices",
            "headline": "First the rules, then the suspect note, then the microphone.",
            "explanation": "An orchestra writes down how much hiss each instrument adds before anyone plays. When someone thinks they hear a wrong note above the middle line, the conductor picks a listening window between the middle line and that note, and only then picks a microphone sharp enough for that window. A perfect microphone with zero hiss is never needed, because every choice is made after the note it has to catch.",
