            "explanation": "The bounds coming from arithmetic lose a little: their exponent is ½ plus a fixed multiple of a small slack ε. Given a candidate zero at height β > ½, you place a threshold θ strictly between ½ and β, then shrink ε until the loss stays below θ. The analytic criterion then excludes the zero. Because ε is picked only after the zero, no bound with exactly zero slack is ever needed.",
