            "title": "Taking off the extra mutes",
            "headline": "A song with a few extra mutes is silent only if the clean song is.",
            "explanation": "Some versions of a song are played with a few extra mutes clipped onto certain strings. Each mute softens the sound but can never silence it completely, and there are only a few of them. So if the clean version never falls silent at some spot, the muted version doesn't either, and the other way round.",
