                "the role of parameter 401 in VWinAt",
                "the proof mechanism transferring window conditions to zero locations",
                "pins: commit, toolchain, Mathlib"
              ],
              "where_metaphor_breaks": "\"Pillar and local checks\" suggests TopG and VWinAt are independent and simple; their actual content and interdependence are fixed only in the formal development and must not be filled in here."
            }
          },
          "L2": {
            "title": "Interface: TopG ∧ (∀ψ primitive: VWinAt ψ 401) → RH ∧ Dirichlet GRH",
            "statement": "Input: (1) the predicate TopG; (2) the family of predicates VWinAt ψ 401 for all primitive Dirichlet characters ψ. Output: the endpoints RH and GRH for Dirichlet L-functions. Invariant: the implication is the Lean theorem Reading.DirichletBridge.endpoints_of_topG_vWin401; all uncertainty sits in the premises.",
            "intuition": "A global cut with two input ports and two output ports. Parameter 401 is fixed in the theorem itself (one value for all ψ), so the input has no hidden free parameters. Quantifying over primitive characters suffices because non-primitive characters are induced by primitive ones.",
            "loss_meter": {
              "fidelity_score": 0.7,
              "compression_ratio": "~10^2:1",
              "topology_status": "faithful_projection",
              "what_is_omitted": [
                "proof internals and intermediate lemmas",
                "Lean types and definitions of TopG and VWinAt",
                "independent-kernel replay status (recorded in formal_core_ir epistemic_status)"
              ],
              "where_metaphor_breaks": "The port framing suggests the inputs are available; neither premise is proved, so RH and GRH are not established here, only reduced to TopG and the window conditions."
            }
          },
          "L3": {
            "title": "TopG and cohomological window conditions VWinAt ψ 401 imply RH and Dirichlet GRH",
            "statement": "Theorem: TopG ∧ ∀ψ primitive: VWinAt ψ 401 ⟹ (all nontrivial zeros of ζ have Re(s) = 1/2) ∧ (for every Dirichlet character χ, all nontrivial zeros of L(s, χ) have Re(s) = 1/2). Formalized in Lean 4 with Mathlib. Premises open; mathematical peer review is independent of machine checking and in progress.",
            "intuition": "Reducing GRH to primitive ψ is standard: for non-primitive χ, L(s, χ) differs from the L-function of its inducing primitive character by a finite product of Euler factors, whose zeros lie on Re(s) = 0 and not in the open critical strip. What is new is the premise shape: one global condition TopG and a uniform (same parameter 401) cohomological-style window condition for each ψ.",
            "loss_meter": {
              "fidelity_score": 0.9,
              "compression_ratio": "~10:1",
              "topology_status": "faithful_projection",
              "what_is_omitted": [
