              "where_metaphor_breaks": "The word \"cohomological\" comes from the cut title; without the archive's definitions one must not assign VWinAt to a specific cohomology theory or read meaning into 401 beyond its being a fixed argument of the predicate."
            }
          },
          "L4": {
            "title": "Reading.DirichletBridge.endpoints_of_topG_vWin401",
            "statement": "Lean identifier: Reading.DirichletBridge.endpoints_of_topG_vWin401. Premise: \\mathrm{TopG}\\ \\wedge\\ \\forall\\psi\\ \\text{primitive}:\\ \\mathrm{VWinAt}\\ \\psi\\ 401. Conclusion: the RH and Dirichlet GRH endpoints. Pins: archive sha256 9631b4f020199e580ba86178cb56c6e9b09f690c2369a80dc4334aa93f49c7fc; PDF sha256 3fc97784b71ddd44ff8aa0a177e99622a1c61b13cfa843a0989ee4a7a0cfeb8d; mirror https://github.com/Deicyde/riemann-hypothesis @ 40e56bab026552e089d7afcfeff08d2defb9c005; toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.33.1; Mathlib 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474.",
            "intuition": "1:1 anchor: an implication, not an unconditional proof. Machine-check status is as recorded in formal_core_ir epistemic_status; human review is a separate, ongoing axis.",
